<br/>
Alongside the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max, which start at &#36;1,199 and &#36;1,299 respectively, Apple now offers the &#36;1,999 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>, its first foldable iPhone. All three feature the A20 Pro chip, but their different designs and capabilities make the decision more complicated than simply choosing a screen size.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s &#36;700 premium over the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max buys a 7.6-inch folding display, Split View multitasking with two apps side by side, and a design that can stand on its own for watching video and making <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> calls. It also supports StandBy without being connected to a charger. These capabilities, alongside the appeal of a radically new kind of iPhone, are its strongest reasons for consideration.<br/>
<br/>
The Pro models offer a more versatile camera system, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a>, the Action button, and substantially lower prices. Our guide helps to answer the question of how to decide which of these iPhones is best for you.<br/>
<br/>
All three models still share a large amount of hardware. The shared features include:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li>A20 Pro chip with a 6-core CPU, 7-core GPU with Neural Accelerators, dual 16-core Neural Engine, and hardware-accelerated ray tracing</li><br/>
<li>Apple C2 modem (except on the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max in the United States), N1 wireless networking chip, and the second-generation Ultra Wideband chip</li><br/>
<li>Super Retina XDR <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> displays with ProMotion up to 120Hz, Always-On display, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, and 3,000 nits of peak outdoor brightness</li><br/>
<li>Ceramic Shield 2 on the Pro models' front displays and the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s outer display, Ceramic Shield backs, and IP68 water and dust resistance to a maximum depth of 6 meters for up to 30 minutes</li><br/>
<li>Camera Control, a 48MP Fusion Ultra Wide camera at 13mm and f/2.2, Photographic Styles 3, Dual Capture, smart focus tracking, and 48MP macro photography</li><br/>
<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI support, subject to feature, language, and regional availability</li><br/>
<li>Emergency SOS, Roadside Assistance, Messages, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/find-my/">Find My</a> via satellite, plus Crash Detection</li><br/>
<li>USB-C with USB 3 speeds, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magsafe/">MagSafe</a> and Qi2 wireless charging up to 25W, and eSIM support</li><br/>
<li>256GB, 512GB, 1TB, and 2TB storage options</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
